{
	title: 'All destructive terminal drawing goes through render.clear(reason)',
	spec: 'Invariant: all destructive drawing in the terminal client goes through one place, render.clear(reason), an exported function on the render module object in src/client/render.ts that returns the erase sequence. Destructive means erasing rows the paint does not rewrite in place: the canonical repaint (CSI 2J H 3J, screen and scrollback), the grow-mode repaint that clears down from the frame top, and erasing leftover rows after a shrink. No other code emits CSI 2J, 3J or a clear-down; a plugin observes every clear with plugin.before(render, \'clear\', (reason) => ...). Clearing to the end of a row being rewritten (CSI 2K) is not destructive. The reason is a plain object naming the cause and its evidence: a forced repaint and its trigger (Ctrl-L or /redraw, resize, resume, tab switch, the first paint with two or more tabs, the top out of reach after the terminal shrank); a frame shrink (old and new row counts, the first changed row, and the blocks whose rows shrank, with block ids such as #t239 and what changed, e.g. tool output collapsed, card closed); or a change to a row already in scrollback (the row, the writable top, the block id and what changed). It also holds one plain-English sentence explaining the snap. Core Hal records nothing: logging is opt-in through a local plugin only. A generic example plugin, a task artifact, appends each reason with the local time and the shown session id as one line to an owner-only (0600) file in the client home state directory, rejects symlinks and keeps the newest 500, so a user can ask a session in the Hal home "why did that snap" and the model answers from that file. Reasons hold no transcript text, tool arguments or output, typed keys, URLs, credentials, hostnames or paths. The reason states which kind of clear it is; only the canonical repaint snaps the user\'s scroll position. Behavioral tests: each clear path calls render.clear with its cause; a shrink names the shrinking block.',
	status: 'planned',
	needs: ['4k'],
	foldInto: ['4k', 'cc']
}
